# Deploy & Release

Production: Docker → nginx stack at `image.sakrylle.com`. Full runbook in Obsidian vault.

## Release gotchas

- **Tag push does NOT reliably trigger GHA** — after tagging, manually: `gh workflow run docker.yml -R Ranshen1209/sakrylle-image --ref theme/sakrylle`
- Bump `package.json` version **and** `public/sw.js` `CACHE_NAME` together
- Image: `ghcr.io/ranshen1209/gpt_image_playground:latest` (GHCR name unchanged)
- Rollback by digest, not `:latest` tag

## Runtime injection (`deploy/inject-api-url.sh`)

| Container env | Placeholder | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `DEFAULT_API_URL` | `__VITE_DEFAULT_API_URL_PLACEHOLDER__` | `https://api.sakrylle.com/v1` |
| `OAUTH_BASE` | `__VITE_SAKRYLLE_OAUTH_BASE_PLACEHOLDER__` | `https://sub.sakrylle.com` |
| `OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` | `__VITE_SAKRYLLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID_PLACEHOLDER__` | `sakrylle-image-playground` |
| `OIDC_ENABLED` | `__VITE_SAKRYLLE_OIDC_ENABLED_PLACEHOLDER__` | `false` |

`ENABLE_API_PROXY=false` (production): strips nginx API proxy block; browser hits api.sakrylle.com directly.

## Verify after deploy

```bash
curl -sS -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" https://image.sakrylle.com/
ssh ssh-tokyo 'docker exec gpt-image-playground sh -c "grep -roh \"https://api.sakrylle.com/v1\" /usr/share/nginx/html/assets | head -1"'
```

## OAuth client (sub2api-owned)

`client_id: sakrylle-image-playground`, `default_group_id=5`. Redirect URIs whitelisted in sub2api `oauth_clients` table — change via psql on sub2api server, not here.
